## Data Model Changes

The chat selector mockup data model evolved from the original `chat-selector-v2.jsx`:

**Original model (nested):**
```
conversation {
  id, title, lastEdited, created, pinned, storageBytes,
  branches: [{ id, title, lastEdited, created, storageBytes }]
}
```

**New model (flat with relationships):**
```
conversation {
  id, title, lastEdited, created, pinned, storageBytes,
  familyId,           // shared ID across parent + all branches (for color grouping)
  parentId,           // null for parents, points to parent for branches
  parentTitle,        // denormalized for display (null for parents)
  aiSummary,          // auto-generated, regenerable
  notes: [{ id, text, messageRef }],  // messageRef = message number or null for general
  highlights: [{ id, text, color, multiline }],
  tags: [string],     // auto-generated from conversation content
}
```

**IndexedDB schema implications:**
- The existing `conversations` store gains: `aiSummary`, `familyId`, `tags` fields
- The existing `notes` store already supports `messageId` (equivalent to `messageRef`)
- The existing `highlights` store needs a `multiline` boolean (or derive it from text length)
- Tags could be a computed field (not stored) or stored for search performance — TBD

